# The Virtual Boy's state goes to PSRAM.
#
# This core was a standalone app until it was folded into retro-core, and folding
# trades one ceiling for another: the flash saving is a whole ~950KB framework
# copy and a partition, but every static the core carries now lands in the same
# internal RAM as the systems already here. video_soft.cpp's texture/character
# cache (tDSPCACHE.CharacterCache and friends) alone is 196608 bytes, and adding
# it was enough to fail the link with esp-idf's "discards section", which is how
# it reports running out of internal RAM (BRINGUP 0.3-2).
#
# legacy_bss (.sbss and friends) has to be routed alongside bss/common: small
# statics are well within RISC-V's gp-relative small-data threshold, and the
# base linker script pulls every object's .sbss into internal RAM unconditionally
# unless the owning archive is placed by a mapping fragment first -- the same
# thing stella's and zxs's folds hit.
#
# The scheme is defined here rather than reusing esp-idf's extram_bss: that one
# lives in esp_wifi's fragment, and this app builds with networking off, so the
# name resolves to nothing -- silently, leaving the link failing at exactly the
# same byte count as before.
[scheme:red_viper_extram]
entries:
    bss -> extern_ram
    common -> extern_ram
    legacy_bss -> extern_ram

[mapping:red_viper_bss]
archive: libred-viper.a
entries:
    * (red_viper_extram)
